{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/256454-crafting-rules","id":256454,"title":"Crafting Rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-13T20:41:51-07:00","id":256454,"title":"Crafting Rules?","content":"Hey, I was curious if anyone has come up with some good solid crafting house rules for Scion since 1st Edition for it fell HOOOOOORIBLY short on covering the crafting of well...anything beyond what is already listed in the book. <br /> <br /> What I believe good crafting rules will need are the following<br /> <br /> 1 - Time Increments - Each type of crafting (Or Art for that Matter) will likely have an extended roll for crafting something, there should be some set idea of how long each roll should take and how many rolls you can make before you have to call it quits because you've either failed or succeeded. <br /> <br /> 2 - Rules for building something from scratch as opposed to just rolling to recreate something from the book. This will be rules for putting stats to things that are not in the book such as Hoplite Armor (By the way, who's the fucking dumbass who dropped the ball on that, not putting stats for one of the most visually recognizable armor in the Roman Army in the book). Or say creating a custom weapon or type of armor from scratch, how many successes will add + whatever to the item. <br /> <br /> 3 - A defined limit as to who can create what level of relic (Thus far what I have done was to say that an individual may craft a Relic that is of the level equal to their Legend/2 but I haven't been able to put it in practice yet). <br /> <br /> Not sure off the top of my head what all else might be needed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"